ECHO OFF
%3
CD \BOARDCHK
CLS
ECHO PYLDIN BOARD CHECK
ECHO Run in the BOARDCHK directory.
ECHO VM and HANDLES 16 must be ready.
ECHO CHECK programs-dir cvm-dir work-drive
ECHO Example: CHECK B: C:\CVM E:
ECHO No RESET during this JOB.
PAUSE
AUTO %1 %2
ECHO OFF
ECHO JCHK06 READY - automatic part done
ECHO Errors in any stage mean failure.
ECHO Next: NC, then F10 to continue.
ECHO MANY: scroll past file 63 and back.
ECHO F4 LONG.TXT: edit, select, undo.
ECHO Save test files in BOARDCHK only.
ECHO Check Ctrl+F1/F2 and input focus.
ECHO Run PLAIN.PGM; check NC returns.
ECHO Ctrl+O, then EXIT: NC must return.
ECHO Test mouse and F-key dialogs.
PAUSE
%1\NC
%3
CD \BOARDCHK
CLS
ECHO JCHK07 READY - PAINT
ECHO F6: mono, 4, 256 colours, HAM8.
ECHO 601A also has 640x200 mono.
ECHO F4 colour; F5 tools; F7/F8 undo.
ECHO Mouse: draw, select, copy, paste.
ECHO Save and reopen TEST.PCX/TEST.IFF.
ECHO F10 returns here; check video.
PAUSE
%1\PAINT
%3
CD \BOARDCHK
CLS
ECHO JCHK08 READY - UART 9600
ECHO F1 Help, Esc closes Help.
ECHO F2 local echo; type some text.
ECHO F3/F4 XMODEM needs a host peer.
ECHO Use test names inside BOARDCHK.
ECHO F10 exits; check no RX errors.
ECHO Test 115200 separately at 8 MHz.
PAUSE
%1\UART 9600
%3
CD \BOARDCHK
CLS
ECHO JCHK CHECK END
ECHO Review all results and visuals.
ECHO Repeat for each CPU/model/speed.
ECHO HD6303: HDCHECK programs-dir %3
ECHO Physical checks are not auto PASS.
ECHO ON
